    "created_at": "2017-02-24T05:22:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-02-24T05:22:10Z",
    "body": "Okay, focus for Shadow DOM is not defined in the HTML spec, though patch exists in Shadow DOM spec - here, we don't have any definition to select *control* if Shadow DOM is involved in `<dialog>`, so we see different levels of problems (of course the former is in higher level in dependency).\r\n\r\nSo does it make sense to change the warning as\r\n\"There is no well defined algorithm yet on selecting *control* if Shadow DOM is used in `<dialog>`.\"?\r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
